## Concrete conclusion and migration proposal

Keeping the Rust library spelling `chitchat` preserves displayed paths but cannot
make the two independently resolved nominal type families interchangeable. The
compiler refusals and TypeId assertions establish that exact limited result.
All internal direct users share one Cargo alias, so a coordinated binding is a
concrete path to test; complete adapter/testkit/raft/sandbox compilation remains
required. External callers explicitly passing/annotating legacy values need their
Cargo dependency coordinated to the maintained identity too.

